'''Le'Grim''' (ジャイアント黒蔵, ''Jaianto Kurozō'', '''Giant Kurozō''') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of [[Le'noir]] unique to the [[Le'Grim Strikes]] event. He was added in [[Version 9.5 Update|Version 9.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Le'Grim
|image = E 510.png
|appearance = [[Le'Grim Strikes]]
|money drop = 1,300¢ - 5,135¢
}}

==Enemy==
Le'Grim has a somewhat long attack cycle, but deals heavy damage from great range, slowing whatever that survives with full uptime. In spite of his low speed, he can push rather easily due to his very short backswing and having only one knockback for his very high health (only losing to Baron Seal and Gigahaniwanwan) in the final stages of his Gauntlet. Much like them, he starts out weak, but recieves extreme buffs in later stages to the point where each attack will eradicate pretty much everything he hits。

Le'Grim, however, has a few notable weaknesses. His support, while annoying, number few in quantity, and can be easily pulled away from him. He is also very vulnerable to Freeze, as his single knockback prevents him from escaping it easily if an opening presents itself, allowing him to be rushed down before support could catch up.

==Strategy==
:''See [[Le'Grim Strikes/Rampage Lv1~20]].''

